From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: usbnet: prevent RX queue starvation and ring deadlock under high throughput

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

Under continuous high-bandwidth mobile tethering (>45MB/s or gigabit bursts),
usbnet's conservative default rx_qlen (13 URBs) can be abruptly exhausted if
transient bus delays occur. When dev->rxq.qlen drops to 0 and dev->delay is
active, the bottom-half processing skips URB refill, creating a permanent ring
deadlock. Furthermore, an unrecovered EVENT_RX_HALT state permanently freezes
the network device.

This MAXNET driver patch:
1. Boosts SuperSpeed rx_qlen to at least 32 URBs (~1MB depth) and tx_qlen to 64 URBs.
2. In rx_alloc_submit(), immediately refills up to RX_QLEN when dev->rxq.qlen == 0.
3. In usbnet_bh(), bypasses the timer_pending throttle check when the queue is
   completely empty (qlen == 0) to avoid interface deadlock.
4. Unconditionally clears EVENT_RX_HALT and schedules bh_work in deferred kevent
   so hardware communication self-heals after temporary USB glitches.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 drivers/net/usb/usbnet.c | 23 +++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/usb/usbnet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/usbnet.c
@@ -375,12 +375,12 @@
 	case USB_SPEED_SUPER:
 	case USB_SPEED_SUPER_PLUS:
 		/*
-		 * Not take default 5ms qlen for super speed HC to
-		 * save memory, and iperf tests show 2.5ms qlen can
-		 * work well
+		 * MAXNET USB 3.0 High-Throughput Pipeline:
+		 * Enforce deep queue depth to prevent RX starvation (>45MB/s)
+		 * Engineered by Mahendra Mali (Max)
 		 */
-		dev->rx_qlen = 5 * MAX_QUEUE_MEMORY / dev->rx_urb_size;
-		dev->tx_qlen = 5 * MAX_QUEUE_MEMORY / dev->hard_mtu;
+		dev->rx_qlen = max_t(int, 32, 10 * MAX_QUEUE_MEMORY / dev->rx_urb_size);
+		dev->tx_qlen = max_t(int, 64, 10 * MAX_QUEUE_MEMORY / dev->hard_mtu);
 		break;
 	default:
 insanity:
@@ -1207,11 +1207,11 @@
 fail_halt:
 				netdev_err(dev->net, "can't clear rx halt, status %d\n",
 					   status);
-		} else {
-			clear_bit (EVENT_RX_HALT, &dev->flags);
-			if (!usbnet_going_away(dev))
-				queue_work(system_bh_wq, &dev->bh_work);
 		}
+		/* MAXNET Self-Healing: Always clear halt and reschedule bottom half */
+		clear_bit (EVENT_RX_HALT, &dev->flags);
+		if (!usbnet_going_away(dev))
+			queue_work(system_bh_wq, &dev->bh_work);
 	}
 
 	/* work could resubmit itself forever if memory is tight */
@@ -1530,11 +1530,12 @@
 static int rx_alloc_submit(struct usbnet *dev, gfp_t flags)
 {
 	struct urb	*urb;
-	int		i;
+	int		i, max_fill;
 	int		ret = 0;
 
-	/* don't refill the queue all at once */
-	for (i = 0; i < 10 && dev->rxq.qlen < RX_QLEN(dev); i++) {
+	/* MAXNET: aggressive queue refill when starved */
+	max_fill = (dev->rxq.qlen == 0) ? RX_QLEN(dev) : 16;
+	for (i = 0; i < max_fill && dev->rxq.qlen < RX_QLEN(dev); i++) {
 		urb = usb_alloc_urb(0, flags);
 		if (urb != NULL) {
 			ret = rx_submit(dev, urb, flags);
@@ -1600,7 +1601,7 @@
 		   netif_device_present (dev->net) &&
 		   netif_carrier_ok(dev->net) &&
 		   !usbnet_going_away(dev) &&
-		   !timer_pending(&dev->delay) &&
+		   (!timer_pending(&dev->delay) || dev->rxq.qlen == 0) &&
 		   !test_bit(EVENT_RX_PAUSED, &dev->flags) &&
 		   !test_bit(EVENT_RX_HALT, &dev->flags)) {
 		int	temp = dev->rxq.qlen;
